[node name="TileMould" type="Area2D" parent="Furniture"]
z_index = 6
position = Vector2(200, -120)
script = ExtResource("10_story_item")
interaction_name = "Look at the Tile Mould"
flag_to_set = ""
discovery_text = "[b]The tile mould[/b]

On a shelf by the workbench, wrapped in oiled leather, sits a two-part stone mould: a row of small blank slabs, each with a hammer over a pine tree cut into its back. The lot tiles for the chapel urn are cast here, from the forge's own iron.

A card is tucked into the leather in Bjorn's blunt hand: 'Each tile two ounces and a half, filed square, name cut once and clean. A lot is only fair if every tile is the same.' Below it, a tally of how many he cast each year, one for every name the council counted."
reexamine_text = "Bjorn's lot-tile mould. 'A lot is only fair if every tile is the same.'"

